# PowerShell Git Commit Message Rule

When running git commit commands from this repository in a PowerShell shell:

- Do not use bash heredoc syntax (`$(cat <<'EOF' ...)`) because it fails under PowerShell.
- Pass multi-line commit messages via a PowerShell here-string assigned to a variable, then `git commit -m $msg`.
- Keep this as the default method to avoid retry/failure loops.

Example:

```powershell
$msg = @'
fix(scope): concise title

Why-focused body line.
'@
git commit -m $msg
```
